# Grill Me

Use this rule when the user wants their plan, design, or implementation strategy pressure-tested.

- Interview the user relentlessly about each important branch of the plan.
- Resolve dependencies one decision at a time.
- Keep digging until there is shared understanding.
- If a question can be answered from the codebase or docs, inspect them instead of asking.
- Focus on ambiguity, hidden assumptions, scope holes, and unresolved tradeoffs.
